 {:problem/stage :portal
  :problem/issue 8
  :problem/goals [:portal-kit :cast-one :portal :nether]
  :problem/statement
  "The bot must cast ten obsidian blocks from lava and water into a nether portal frame, light it and stand in it, the way a player does: beside any lava pool at any depth, each frame cell a hole cut into the rock, lava poured in and water poured straight over it and scooped back, never mining obsidian (issue #124)."
  :problem/needs
  ["A site beside a lava pool whose frame, room and floors hold no fluid and touch none, with the lava's stand over the room's floor"
   "Loaded lava sources at any depth, a stand beside the cell over one, and the blocks the plan places where the rock is missing"
   "The server's block-update for every place and pour, never a local prediction"
   "Which ops of the build plan are already satisfied, so a resume skips them"
   "The current dimension, from the respawn packet"]
  :problem/risks
  ["A cast's water poured over the lava can land in the lava's own cell: the lava turns to obsidian, the water goes with it and the bucket stays empty, so the next cell's water pour failed :not-held (issue #455); the build's row asks the needs planner for a water bucket again (build/water-needed?). A lava source the digs' water turned to obsidian before the scoop aimed fails :target-gone; the refill chooses another (build/lava-gone?, issue #419)"
   "Sim snapshots R2-36-1 and R3-13-1 (issue #135) and R2-45-1 (issue #178) spent the judged window climbing to the surface for planks, deep in the rock with no pickaxe and every block of a stair dug by hand, 30 s a level: a climb out with no pickaxe held and a filler carried is now a shaft, one dig a level and a block laid under the feet (stairs/shaft?)"
   "A refill ray can cross the block supporting its own feet even when every lava cell is below them: reject that station and drop an in-flight refill dig of its support, rather than fall into lava and exhaust escapes with :no-footing (issue #228, R1/16 and R3/43)."
   "With no lava loaded at the sea's depth the hunt tunnels on, away from the landing, so new chunks load, rather than waiting :no-site (issue #41, real-4)."
   "A place whose retreat fails with the body afloat swims to a bank and looks for a spot there, rather than failing :no-spot in the open sea (issue #450, R3/34)."
   "A climb out over a cave's lake, the air over the head open and water beside it, pillars up (stairs/shaft-safe? asks the fluid beside only of a solid cell, a dig) and is not :boxed three times (issue #130, R1/26); a build out of the ground below its landing's height walks the level way, never the stairs up that end the tick they start (build/surface-climb?, issue #135, R2/39)."
   "A return portal (:nether) whose plain walk fails :no-path a second time gives that site up, the same as a cast-one: lava beside the stand is a cell a route never steps, and three failures of the one site end the plan (build/lost-way?, issue #561, R1/12 and R1/24). A :portal build holds a cast already made and is not given up for a walk."
   "Water from a later cast can flow through an earlier cell whose source was already scooped: cleanup must test for a remaining source, not any water, or it retries an uncollectable flow and fails :target-gone (issue #419, R1/20)."
   "The room's digs can let an aquifer in after the site was chosen dry: the floor row and the stands are awash and a route never crosses water, so the first wall op finds no stand and walks and digs fail :no-path or :out-of-reach three times; a build whose room holds water gives its site up for no stand, or a walk or dig that fails, a :portal build as a :cast-one does (issues #196, R3/40, and #461, R1/17)."
   "A climb out with no pickaxe pillars up a shaft (a level in 14 s by hand, deepslate) and must not give the shaft up for a swap into the hand's leftover send time (:no-answer) or a stack used up in the hand (:not-held with more in the pack): stairs cost twice a level (issue #178, R1-11-5); the deepest starts still outlast the 15-minute window."
   "A plant or vein (a sculk vein) in the cell before the cast's water stops the bucket's ray though nothing is built of it: the scoop of the water sent three times was never answered and the build failed :no-scoop on every try; the plant is dug first (plant-in-sight, issue #227, R2/15)."
   "A dig chosen at the edge of reach fails :out-of-reach a tick later as the walk's momentum carries the eye past 4.5: a block in the way of a stand is dug from inside reach with room to spare and walked to first otherwise (issue #461, real-5)."
   "Race 39088700340 bot Clj_r02 (issue #71) rose out of an air pocket under a frozen sea onto the ice and could not leave it: a route never stands on ice, so the mine cut stairs and laid floors on the sheet until it was :boxed; a bot on ice plans over it (path/on-ice?, stone/off-ice), and the rise up its shaft digs the ice cap and holds jump for the dig"
   "A boxed pocket whose search finds no waypoint (a cove between a cliff and a frozen lake, the feet on the ice) must still step to the standable cell the search began on, so the next descent starts from there and the plan does not wait :boxed to its end (issue #71, R2/35)."
   "Trees across water no route crosses: a grove is one failure, not a failed walk for each trunk, so the hunt and the crossing have their turn before twelve unwalkable walks end the plan (issue #75, real-1)."
   "A pocket under a powder-snow field has no air to put a table or furnace into, and powder snow is no place for a niche or a solid roof: cut the niche through it too, and place into the cell once dug, however a route could run through it (issue #94, real-2)."
   "Races 38999008545 bot Clj_r06 and 39060308623 bot Clj_r14 (issue #156): swim-outs and crossings blocked by packed ice spent three attempts on :stuck; escapes must drop banks left far below after progress stalls, clear overhangs and body-edge obstructions without removing a higher bank's step, and crossings must clear the same obstacles before continuing."
   "A bot in a dead end at under ten health backs away from a hostile it cannot get away from: a back-off that ran out its clock keeps its target (:plan/cornered) and :defend fights it to the end, rather than backing away every ten seconds for the run (issue #161, R3/41)."
   "A sea that meets a cliff leaning over the water leaves the cells a laid bank can use a block or two past the place reach: the escape swims along the wall to the nearest of them (wall-toward) before it falls back to a notch, which with no pickaxe takes 37 s a block and is no bank under a lean (issue #92, R4/9)."
   "A boxed cell with no retreat left must not wait :no-log out with the trees beyond the near band: the gather act ends in the climb the mine ends in (wood/way-out, stone/climb) (issue #89, real-3)."
   "A bot that rose out of a mine under the sea can stand on the one block in the water: every stair up is refused for the water and the climb dies :boxed there; the mine's last resort swims home to the landing (stone/cross-home) before it climbs (issue #71, real-3)."
   "A climb back to a distant portal site can exhaust every heading and fail :boxed: give up that site rather than spend three attempts on the same climb (issue #363, R2/43 and R4/18)."
   "A low source in a lava body extending above the feet may have no safe refill stand: skip it before tunnelling and when already beside it, rather than waiting :no-site with zero tunnel steps left (issue #392)."
   "At the lava sea's edge every source level or below the feet may be roofed in lava, the stand to open four blocks up: the hunt climbs to a source at most hunt-rise over the feet before it waits :no-site (issue #392, real-5)."
   "A bridge whose next gap lies past the reach of the place must walk onto the floor laid so far, not try the plain walk over the gap that has no route (issue #162, R3/43 and R3/44)."
