 {:problem/stage :blaze-rods
  :problem/issue 262
  :problem/goals [:blaze-rods]
  :problem/statement
  "Split from :end-and-dragon. Seven blaze rods (six for the twelve blaze powder the eyes of ender take, one spare), from blazes a fortress's spawner makes, without dying to their fireballs: the first stage past the fortress, and the first whose loot may not come (a rod one kill in two)."
  :problem/needs
  ["Where a blaze spawner is: a spawner seen in the Nether is a fortress's, remembered after its chunk unloads (memory/nether-landmark-kinds)"
   "Which blazes are near and alive, and how hurt the bot is (entity.clj, set-health)"
   "Which drop on the ground is a rod: a dropped item's stack from its metadata (index 8)"
   "A pickup that is done when nothing lies there to pick up, since a kill may drop nothing (:collect-drops)"
   "A fight that reaches a target hovering over the floor (combat/pressing?)"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Fireballs: five a hit on Normal, and fire; a bot that fights on under 10 health dies with the blaze (ruststeve)"
   "The burning after a fireball and standing in fire kill more than the hits (blaze-race-f and -g, damage by type: on_fire 7 to 45, in_fire up to 26, fireball 3 to 10 a run): a shield in the offhand blocks from the front, and fire at the feet is left first"
   "Fighting in the open: nine of twenty deaths in blaze-race-g and -i fought or backed off while burning or under a volley, three stood frozen: the bot fights from a pocket, a cell with one opening and a firm roof found or dug into a wall (pocket.clj), holds there while burning or under engage-health, strikes only what comes to reach, raises the shield only there, and routes through no fire block"
   "A hold open in the pocket under fire (blaze-race-j race 3 and race 1: blazes at 4.0 and 5.4, out of reach, in line): the pocket is sealed with cobblestone while it burns or is pressed, held, then opened; a failed :pocket is a here-site sealed in place, never a failed plan; the pocket is dug in the tunnel's wall before its last blocks open"
   "Fighting until death (blaze-race-k: 10 of 10 dead, the two that lived 15 to 25 minutes held 2 rods): under 12 hp or after a second ignition within 30 s the bot goes to its pocket (or seals the cell it stands in), is held there until 20 hp and the fire out, and a running tunnel is cut for it; a walk out of a fire ends in its cell and a bot sealed in with a fire punches it out; the shield is dropped (0 of 16 fireball hits landed with it up)"
