 {:problem/stage :sim-mobs-and-end
  :problem/issue 260
  :problem/goals []
  :problem/statement
  "The server model has no hunger, no mobs, no eye of ender and no End, so the sim lanes play an easier game than the real races at Normal, and nothing past the Nether can be played against the model; every stage after the fortress needs the model to play it first."
  :problem/needs
  ["Hunger as FoodData keeps it: exhaustion from jumps, digs, hits and heals, saturation first, regeneration at 18, starvation to 1 health on Normal, eating a held food for 32 ticks"
   "The server's difficulty as an input, absent for snapshots kept before it, so they play as they did"
   "Mobs that spawn by a seeded rule (night, dark cells, a cap), walk straight at the player and hurt it; creepers that fuse and blast; skeletons that shoot at range; an attack that hurts them by the held item and kills them with their loot"
   "Mob fixtures (:sim/mobs given) for every combat stage's sim tests"
   "An eye of ender thrown with use-item that flies toward the stronghold as a real eye does"
   "The End: arrival on the obsidian platform, end portal frames that take eyes and light the portal, a perched dragon with 200 health and crystals on their pillars"]
  :problem/risks
  ["A model that sends a packet shape the bot's specs reject, once the mob model's specs land (#258)"
   "Hunger or mobs in the unit tests' worlds changing what every older test sees"
   "Mob ticks slowing the 2,000-world property or the sim lanes"
   "A model easier than the server (no blast, no arrows) hiding real deaths, or harder (mobs through walls) making false failures"]
  :problem/done
  "sim tests for each mechanic pass against the model, and the sim lanes' runs show deaths and foods eaten (:run/respawns, :run/eaten)."
  :problem/last-failure
  "The first deaths in the sim lanes were each an enderman the bot provoked just outside its burrow and then fought, not the model."
  :problem/seen [{:issue 260 :run "39848524906"}]
  :problem/sources ["brain/bot/tooling/server-model.md" "docs/RICH-HICKEY.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :mob-model
  :problem/issue 258
  :problem/goals [:entities]
  :problem/statement
  "Split from :end-and-dragon. The world value tracks item drops only, so no goal can see a mob, how fast it moves, how hurt it is, or that it died; every fight after this needs that, read from the server and never predicted."
  :problem/needs
  ["Every add-entity kept, with its velocity" "set-entity-motion and teleport-entity applied"
   "A living entity's health and shared flags from set-entity-data, skimmed"
   "Which entity types are living (only they have health at the metadata's index 9), from the game's classes"
   "Death as a fact: entity-event status 3, then the removal"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["Velocity is the game's LpVec3, read from the jar (probe run 38876275250), not three shorts in 1/8000 blocks"
   "The metadata skim reads only simple serializers and stops at the first other, keeping what it read"
   "Living types and their maximum health come from DefaultAttributes by jar-probe (mobs.edn), never a hand list"
   "Hostile is the game's monster category minus the neutral ones (enderman, zombified piglin)"]
  :problem/risks ["A pig beside a drop taken for the drop now that every entity is tracked"
                  "An interaction's or a boat's float at index 9 read as health"
                  "A custom name (a component) before the health ends the skim"
                  "Metadata or motion for the bot's own player, which is never added"]
  :problem/done
  "The gym's entities row: a summoned pig's health in the bot's world value equals RCON data get entity on it, RESULT :ok true."
  :problem/last-failure
  "The last failure was a trial that ended on a natural pig's health; it now ends only on a living entity within 4 blocks."
  :problem/seen [{:issue 258 :run "38880450846"} {:issue 258 :run "38881512647"}]
  :problem/sources ["docs/RICH-HICKEY.md" "brain/bot/world/entities.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :race
  :problem/issue 17
  :problem/statement
  "One bot proves a stage once; a pass rate needs many bots from many starts at once. The runners give twenty servers of 16 GB and four cores, each of which can carry the server and several bots, and the bots must not get in each other's way: two on one forest share its trees and its ground."
  :problem/needs
  ["Each bot its own world value, loop, socket and recording, exactly as one bot runs alone, so a racer's run replays alone"
   "One thing shared, the landing cells, as values on one bounded channel, folded first come first served"
   "A landing per bot on ground of its own: a forest near a cell no other bot holds, judged by the server's answers"
   "Every step from empty hands to the target in play, the reached ones staying reached (a chained run)"
   "A different world on each runner, so twenty runners are twenty starts and not one start twenty times"
   "A measure of how many bots a server carries: its tick time, read while the race runs"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Fresh players generating chunks at once time each other out (steve's races 610 and 611 ghosted after their teleports)"
   "Too many bots for four cores: the server's ticks stretch and every bot's timing with them"
   "Two bots claiming one forest" "A crashed racer taking the others down with it"
   "Reconnecting bots colliding with themselves (steve: relaunch without killing the old race halved its throughput)"]
  :problem/done
  "On every runner a RESULT line per bot and a RACE summary; a bot that reached the target is confirmed by the server (data get entity <name> Dimension reads the Nether); no cell granted twice."
  :problem/last-failure
  "The last failure was an intent chosen again every 50 ms while the bot stood still; the planner now counts that churn and a guard checks it."
  :problem/decisions
  ["One JVM per runner, a thread per bot (main/run-bot!): one bot's whole life is a function, so many run side by side, each its own atom; no process per bot"
   "The fixture claims for each bot, through the claims channel, and speaks to the bot only through its own bounded event queue"
   "Cells are 96 blocks square from where the first bot joins; the forest nearest a cell's middle is claimed by the cell it lies in"
   "keep_inventory on, as the siblings race; peaceful, as the full run"]
  :problem/sources ["docs/RICH-HICKEY.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :ender-pearls
  :problem/issue 263
  :problem/goals [:ender-pearls :ender-pearl :spare-picks]
  :problem/statement
  "Split from :end-and-dragon. Twelve eyes of ender need twelve ender pearls, and bartering for them takes far more gold than the run mines, so the bot hunts endermen: find one, make it come, kill it with the sword and live, pick up the pearl it drops one time in two, about twenty-four times."
  :problem/needs
  ["The endermen round the bot, alive or dead, from the mob model (#258)"
   "The pearl drop rate, read from the game's own loot table, which sets how many kills the stage costs"
   "Whether a look at an enderman provokes it, and when an angry one teleports, from the game's classes"
   "A clear line from the eye to an enderman's head, from the terrain"
   "Where a kill fell, to pick its drop up"
   "Armour worn and a sword in hand before the first fight (#259)"
   "Where the warped forests are: a fact a chunk (memory/forest-fact: forest-min or more blocks of warped nylium), kept after the chunk unloads. The race leaves the bot at a fortress; only the gym lands it in a forest (RCON locate biome)"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["Hunt, never barter (issue #263): a stack of gold per twelve pearls is a mine the run never makes"
   "The loot table is one roll of ender_pearl, count uniform 0 to 1, plus 0 to 1 a level of looting (probe run 38889277228): a pearl a kill one time in two"
   "A warped forest is the hunting ground: its only monster spawner is the enderman, four at a time (the same probe)"
   "Provoke by a stare at the head from 6 blocks or more, then look at its legs: an angry enderman stared at within 4 teleports away, one stared at within 16 stands frozen, and a melee hit by the bot never teleports it (EnderMan.hurtServer, EndermanLookForPlayerGoal)"
   "Fight from a burrow, not in the open: three stairs down and a tunnel two high, the enderman stopped at the last stair two cells off, out of its reach (a mob's melee is its box grown 0.83 sideways, never up or down: Mob.getAttackBoundingBox, probe run 38893918055) and inside the sword's; the open fight is only the fallback where no burrow can be cut. Never from water, which the escapes already forbid"
   "The rows stay asides until the stages before them are proven; raising the chain to them is its own change"
   "Travel to a warped forest before the hunt (pearls/travel): the cell over the nearest known forest nylium, else explore; only in the Nether, only with no enderman tracked, never hurt, swarmed or menaced. Chosen over decoding the chunk's biome container because the memory already watches blocks and a per-chunk fact of the nylium count needs no biome table; the gym row pearls-12-from-fortress starts where the race does (issue #263, real race 40980342194 Clj_r13: two hours round a fortress, no pearl)"
   "Exit the fortress after blaze rods by retracing the inbound path through enclosed cells, boring a parallel 1x2 tunnel through solid netherrack or brick beside open corridors at the same y, and forbidding downward steps (no dy < 0) to avoid punching through thin fortress floors over the lava sea (issue #263, #715)"
   "A retrace or side-bore target is never within 2 blocks of the feet: a tunnel to a cell inside its reach (1.5) ends :done without a step and is chosen again every tick (issue #263, race run 41781768766 Clj_r79: 24,234 :tunnel-to starts on its own feet cell after the rods, 3 cells dug, cut by the lane still in the spawner pocket)"
   "Leave the fortress from the sealed blaze pocket, not the open spawner floor: seal the pocket and heal to full in it first, then bore along one fixed heading (from the spawner toward the inbound trail's start) digging only cells whose neighbours are solid, side-stepping at the same y rather than opening into air or a corridor, sealing behind and never digging down, surfacing only beyond 48 blocks from every spawner and brick; when hit while boring, seal the current cell and heal before going on (issue #263, run 41852247420: Clj_r32 flipped between two retrace targets 45 times wearing its pickaxe out, Clj_r36 dug 9 s a cell in the blazes' sight, Clj_r12 and Clj_r13 died after a rejected seal left no cover)"
   "Leave the fortress from the sealed blaze pocket, not the open spawner floor: seal the pocket and heal to full in it first, then bore along one fixed heading (from the spawner toward the inbound trail's start) digging only cells whose neighbours are solid, side-stepping at the same y rather than opening into air or a corridor, sealing behind and never digging down, surfacing only beyond 48 blocks from every spawner and brick; when hit while boring, seal the current cell and heal before going on (issue #263, run 41852247420: Clj_r32 flipped between two retrace targets 45 times wearing its pickaxe out, Clj_r36 dug 9 s a cell in the blazes' sight, Clj_r12 and Clj_r13 died after a rejected seal left no cover)"
   "After the seventh rod the blaze refuge stays in charge while any blaze watches, at full health too: measured on the 2026-11-04 races (6d16500), 20 of 21 real rod bots held 15 to 20 health at the rod with blazes in sight, bored out in their sight under the hunt, were shot down and only then sent back, the pocket-go and the bore cutting each other until the blazes killed 17 of 21; and the walk to the blaze nook ends standing in its cell (intent/standing-walks :nook), since at-nook? counts only that cell and a walk ended beside it churned to :instant-churn (Clj_r98, Clj_r56, Clj_r62)"
   "Make spare stone pickaxes before leaving the fortress after the blaze rods (issue #263): while sealed and safe in the blaze pocket, craft stone pickaxes to hold three using carried table, sticks and cobblestone; make more whenever safe and down to one in the hunt, taking the placed table along and dropping one junk stack when sealed so a pearl drop has room (real race Clj_r22 run 41936905595 wore its one pickaxe out boring to the forest and dug bare-handed at 6250 ms a block)"
   "Go toward a distant enderman sighting (issue #263, race-read 1105b on 0ace52e): every first sighting of 23 real rod bots was 54 to 105 blocks off, past hunt-radius 32, so the hunt never acted and provoked 0 of 141; a safe rod bot out of the fortress (not under danger health, no blaze watching) now goes toward the nearest tracked sighting within 128 to a reachable stand near it (never its own cell, a stand on its level for one 20 to 60 above or below), by walk, by a walk as far as the route goes, or by a sealed level tunnel, giving the sighting up after three failed goes or five minutes so it never churns"
   "Never idle the pearl stage (issue #263): 42 of 141 real rod bots on 0ace52e ended :nothing-to-do with time and health left; when every hunt row is nil the stage falls back to the sighting chase, else the forest search or exit it already has (travel, explore), else a lookout - never a planner wait with nothing pending"
   "Bound the blaze refuge after the rods (issue #263): 22 of 52 sim rod bots timed out at the spawner pocket fighting and collecting for hours because #723's watcher gate keeps the refuge in charge while a blaze watches and the spawner never stops spawning; once sealed full, or held at full health for three minutes since the refuge first kept it, the bot leaves by the sealed fortress tunnel-out even with a watcher, fighting only what blocks the way, while the first minutes after rod 7 keep #723's protection; the spawner is never broken and no bot fights under danger health"
   "The fortress exit tunnel bridges a cavern as the way to the fortress does (issue #263, real stage-18 lanes on ba1e8b7, runs 42576015140 42576244600 42576461618 42576586054): 9 of the 10 :blocked endings were the exit tunnel, and those folded to the failing tick stood on a column of its own blocks in open Nether air, its surface target fifty blocks along and higher, every level and up step over air and no-down? refusing the steps down, so it failed :blocked from the same stand 43 to 102 times until the plan stalled at fifteen minutes, with no pearl; a level step floored from the block under the feet, over ground, at bridge-min-health and with a reserve of filler (fortress/bridge-over-void?), and still never a step down"
   "Leave a piglin brute's ground, never hide beside it (issue #263, real forest-start lane 6 on 9bcac74, run 42628418702, and lane 5 on 4170b7d, run 42628090070): five bots died to brutes 10 to 30 blocks from their landing, three golden-axe hits of 9.1 through iron and gold boots in two to eight seconds, after one to two minutes of cover-from-swarm digs, walls and pillars within earshot of them; a brute strikes any player, gold worn or not, and keeps to its bastion, so a brute within brute-radius 24 sends the hunt on a walk to the far end farthest from it (else a back-off), and every square a brute was seen in is kept brute-clear 32 from any walk's end afterwards"
   "Never break or open what piglins guard with one near (issue #263, real stage-18 on 4170b7d, run 42627593590 Clj_r06): gold boots worn and no swing, its fortress exit tunnel broke nether_gold_ore at [845 57 -220] and the piglin within ten blocks turned on it the same tick; Clj_r11 (run 42627421412) dug only netherrack under a cluster of seven nether gold ore and no block near it changed, its anger unexplained. A dig or an open of a guarded_by_piglins block (threats.edn :guarded) with a piglin or brute within 16 fails :guarded"]
  :problem/risks
  ["Seven a hit on Normal, one hit a second, against forty health: an iron sword needs seven hits, so a fight in the open costs most of the bot's health even in iron"
   "The bot staring at an enderman's face by accident (a look at its head from within 4 blocks) sends it away mid-fight"
   "An enderman carrying a block drops the block beside its pearl: only a drop that says it holds a pearl (#262's :entity/item), or has not said yet, may be picked up"
   "No warped forest near where the bot comes out of the portal" "Endermen teleporting out of reach"
   "The way to a forest: lava seas, ghasts, crimson forests full of hoglins and piglins, endless travel with no forest known (explore widens along a heading, never to ground already arrived at)"]
  :problem/done
