 {:problem/stage :eyes-of-ender
  :problem/issue 264
  :problem/goals [:eyes-of-ender]
  :problem/statement
  "Split from :end-and-dragon. Twelve eyes of ender, one for each frame of the end portal, crafted from the rods and pearls the two stages before hold: blaze powder from a rod (two a rod), an eye from a powder and a pearl, both in the 2x2 grid with no table."
  :problem/needs
  ["The two recipes as data: blaze_powder (shapeless, one rod, two powder) and ender_eye (shapeless, a pearl and a powder), already generated craft rows (make/craft-rows)"
   "The held rods, powder, pearls and eyes, from the inventory the server sent"
   "What is short when the eyes cannot be made, named for its stage: :no-pearls or :no-rods (eyes/lacking)"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["Twelve, not fourteen: the pearl stage makes twelve, and the throws that find the stronghold (an eye breaks one throw in five) are the stronghold stage's to count, from pearls it asks for then"
   "No producer for a rod or a pearl in the needs planner: each is its own stage with its own rules (blaze.clj, pearls.clj), so a short eye stage waits and names it"
   "An aside at priority 20 after the pearls, so the run's current stage stays the fortress until the stages before it are proven"]
  :problem/risks
  ["A craft click lost or answered late on a loaded server, as at the kit (window/lost, window/resync)"
   "The inventory full, so a powder or an eye has nowhere to go"
   "Rods or pearls spent or lost between their stages and this one: a chained run does not go back for them"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON: clear <bot> minecraft:ender_eye 0 finds twelve or more after seven rods and twelve pearls are given on a surface landing (gym eyes)."
  :problem/last-failure
  "No failure recorded; the gym batch passed 6/6 with twelve eyes held 20 to 30 s after landing."
  :problem/seen [{:issue 264 :run "38920108562"}]
