 {:problem/stage :end-portal
  :problem/issue 266
  :problem/goals [:end-portal :enter-end]
  :problem/statement
  "Split from :end-and-dragon. In the stronghold's portal room, with eyes of ender held, put an eye into each of the twelve frames that lacks one so the portal lights, then step into it and arrive in the End on the obsidian platform without walking off it into the void."
  :problem/needs
  ["Which frames lack an eye: the frame's state (end/eyed?), read from the loaded block, else the last sighting"
   "A cell the feet can stand in within reach of each frame that a route reaches: the frames float two blocks over the room's floor round a 3x3 pit of lava, so the far side of the ring is reached by walking on the frames themselves, 13/16 high, which a route must take for floors"
   "The way up to the frames from the room's floor: three stairs blocks with a silverfish spawner in the middle of the top step, so a route must climb stairs, a block at a time, up a side"
   "When the portal is lit: the server places the nine end portal blocks the moment the twelfth eye goes in (EndPortalFrameBlock.useItemOn); they are remembered like the frames"
   "When the End is reached: the respawn packet naming minecraft:the_end sets :player/dimension"
   "What takes the body into the portal: the end portal block has no collision, so feet over it drop into its cell, and the server moves the player at once (no four-second wait as at a nether portal)"]
  :problem/risks
  ["A use-item while looking at a frame fills it: the throw trial looks up; here the look is at the frame on purpose, and a use-item-on on a frame that has its eye only acks"
   "Walking the ring: a misstep into the interior before the portal is lit is a fall of two into lava; the route refuses cells beside or over lava (path/clear?), and the frames are its only floors there"
   "A frame reached from under it, from the room's floor, is out of reach: the eye is 2.6 under the frame's top"
   "The ring on record is not whole: a frame's chunk unloaded or a frame unseen; the enter row waits :no-ring"
   "In the End the platform stands over the void: a route off its edge finds no landing and is refused, and the bot stands still once the row is done"
   "Endermen in the End and the dragon's first flight: nothing of this stage fights; the dragon is #267's"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["The work is a plan of ops read against the world each tick (build/work-op), as the nether portal's cast: the first frame without an eye is worked, so a death or a reload resumes where the world says, and nothing records progress"
   "The frames, the end portal and stairs are floors to a route (path/stood-on), since the physics' oracle already takes each for a full cube and the feet read their cell a half block up: a player walks the frames and climbs the stairs, and so does the bot"
   "The gym builds the vanilla portal room itself (gym/portal-room, StrongholdPieces.PortalRoom block for block, the frames facing inward as the game's own do) round a surface landing and lands the bot on the room's floor inside its door: locate structure names a stronghold's start, not its portal room, and no command finds the room; the real room is the stronghold stage's to reach (#265)"
   "The enter row's ops are the end portal row's and then a wait for the nine portal blocks and the step in: one plan builder with an enter? flag, as frame-plan takes one"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON: an end_portal block at the cell the bot remembers one (gym end-portal, :truth/at [:portal]); the bot in minecraft:the_end (gym enter-end, gym/dimension-test). sim_test: against the model's End, every frame eyed and nine portal cells placed; the dimension flips and the player stands on the platform."
  :problem/last-failure
  "No failure recorded in the gym; the open question is the way to a real stronghold room, which is the stronghold stage's."
  :problem/seen [{:issue 266 :run "39132430055"}]
  :problem/sources ["brain/siblings/sib-end-and-dragon.md"]}
 {:problem/stage :dragon
  :problem/issue 267
  :problem/goals [:crystals :dragon :heal]
  :problem/statement
  "Split from :end-and-dragon. In the End, break the ten end crystals that heal the dragon, each on top of an obsidian spike 76 to 103 high, without dying to the blast a hit sets off, then kill the dragon with the sword while it perches on the fountain, and know from the server that it died."
  :problem/needs
  ["Every end crystal and the dragon in the entity map, with where they stand (add-entity, entity/kind)"
   "A way up a spike with no bow: a pillar of blocks beside it, a block put under the feet at the top of each jump once the body is clear of the cell"
   "A stand within reach of the crystal whose line to the blast is shut: the crystal blasts with power 6 at any hit, about 56 damage three blocks off with a clear line, so two blocks go between the body and it"
   "A way back down: the pillar dug from its top, a block at a time, never a fall"
   "When the dragon perches: its position held within six of the fountain (0, 0) and under y 70, and its box (16 by 8, its feet on the pillar) in reach of the eye"
   "The dragon's breath (area_effect_cloud) and fireballs (dragon_fireball) near the feet"
   "The win as the server says it: entity-event 3 on the dragon, its removal with no boss bar shown (boss-event), or game-event win_game (answered with client-command 0)"]
  :problem/risks
  ["A crystal struck in the open kills the bot: no wall but the one the bot put there stops the blast"
   "A wide spike (radius 3 to 5) puts the crystal out of reach from beside it: the stand is on the spike's top, walked onto from the pillar"
   "Two spikes have iron cages round their crystals: the walk onto them is shut, and a strike through the bars is unproven"
   "A block placed while the body is still in the cell is refused, and the jump lands back where it was"
   "Endermen in the End turn on a bot that looks them in the face; a hit on a pillar is a fall"
   "The dragon's charges and fireballs between perches; its body takes a quarter of a hit plus one, and after 50 damage in one perch it takes off"
   "The dragon flown out of the bot's tracking taken for dead: a removal counts only near the bot with no boss bar"
   "The End's platform floats over the void at x 100: the main island is a bridge away, and nothing of this stage builds one"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["The strike stands three out from the crystal's column along an axis, feet level with the spike's top, with two blocks in the cell between at the feet's height and the eye's: the crystal's box is two away, and every line from the blast to the body crosses the blocks. Along an axis only, so the two cells cover the body"
   "The pillar goes up the first column out from the spike's top layer along that axis, never nearer than the stand: on a spike of radius 2 its top is the stand"
   "Everything is read from the world each tick (the nearest crystal, its approach, whether the feet stand on two pillar blocks or three obsidian), so a death or a reload resumes where the world says and nothing records progress"
   "The bot waits for the perch in the exit portal's basin two out from the pillar: the sitting dragon turns its face to the bot, its head 6.5 out and its neck 5.5, and both hurt what they touch"
   "While the dragon sits, the stand is one behind its body (its yaw, :entity/yaw, the head along (sin yaw, -cos yaw)), re-chosen when the head comes onto the feet, and a walk goes round the head, never under it: two out in front, the head lowered to the bot brings the neck over the stand"
   "Every look of the dragon row's intents, walks and back-offs too, is turned from an enderman's eyes (plan/steer); in a lull the bot eats for health back under food 18 (the :heal row)"
   "While the dragon sits or lands (phases 3, 5, 6, 7) the bot stays on the basin's floor, under the head's and neck's reach, which come down to the rim: a breath near the feet is answered inside the basin (the walk to a stand out of its reach, else the perch held), any other breath by a walk to the nearest cell out of every breath's reach and not before the head (never a straight back-off, which ran into the fountain's pillar and died in the cloud), the scanning turn (phase 6) is held still through and a new stand taken only in the phases the dragon does not turn in, and the :defend row leaves every hostile to this row while a breath reaches the feet, the back-off from it first"
   "The perched dragon is struck by its box, not by :fight's aim point: the server tests an attack's reach to the box, and an aim point over feet on the fountain's pillar is out of reach from every floor"
   "The gym takes the cages away and puts a crystal on each spike's bedrock with the dragon gone, so the crystals row measures the pillar and the strike; the dragon row has no crystals and a summoned dragon (DragonPhase 0, which the End's fight takes for its own on the bot's arrival)"]
  :problem/done
  "RCON: execute in minecraft:the_end unless entity @e[type=minecraft:end_crystal] passes (gym crystals: ten put on the spikes, all gone); execute in minecraft:the_end unless entity @e[type=minecraft:ender_dragon] passes (gym dragon: summoned, dead, RESULT :ok true). sim_test: against the model's End, a crystal on a spike broken from behind a wall with no blast taken and the bot back down; the perched dragon killed and :world/dragon-dead? set."
  :problem/last-failure
  "The last failures were tunnel searches that timed out the server keep-alive and a dragon fight begun at low health; searches are now bounded."
