 {:problem/stage :real-snapshots
  :problem/issue 299
  :problem/goals []
  :problem/statement
  "A real race's failure leaves only a recording that replays what happened: the server's half is frozen in the file, so no fix can be judged against it, and half the failures the races find (the real-only issues) have no evidence a pull request's check can judge."
  :problem/needs
  ["The bot's world at any moment of a real run: the recording folded with the reducer that made it"
   "The terrain the server sent, byte for byte (every level-chunk-with-light is in the file), and the blocks changed since (the bot's overlay)"
   "The server's view of the player at that moment, as far as the bot was told: window 0, health, food, the held place, the state id, its entity id, the entities it tracks"
   "A moment chosen before the choice that failed, as a sim run's is, where the model can join (no container open)"]
  :problem/risks
  ["A fold by other code is another run (#111): the churn must convert at the race's own commit"
   "What the bot never heard (the time of day, a closed furnace, the hunger clock, the respawn point, entities the model does not model) making the model answer otherwise"
   "A real snapshot filed as evidence when the model does not reproduce it: a fix would be judged against a failure the model never had"
   "A snapshot over GitHub's 100 MiB file limit"]
  :problem/decisions
  ["The model joined mid-play from data (sim/joined), the bot's world translated in real.clj; no handshake"
   "Columns by the bytes the recording holds, the held ones as the bot decoded them, within a captured world's radius; never re-encoded"
   "Self-contained: the columns ride in the snapshot (:snapshot/columns), so the check restores no world"
   "Kept only when it recurs with the same code; a gap is printed with how the bot got past, never filed"]
  :problem/done
  "A recorded real failure from a lane becomes a snapshot on a runner that recurs on main's code with JUDGE and STORY lines matching the recording, and the real rounds' comments list real snapshots that bb issue-check fetch takes."
  :problem/last-failure
  "The last failure was a judge that ran so near its time budget that a verdict was not evidence; such a verdict is now a :slow gap."
  :problem/seen [{:issue 299 :run "38929353563"} {:issue 299 :run "38948145791"}]
  :problem/sources ["brain/bot/tooling/real-snapshots.md" "docs/RICH-HICKEY.md"]}]
